(a) When any life safety system (e.g., sprinkler system or fire alarm system) of any facility required by the Life Safety Code to have such systems is, or will be out of service for a period of more than four hours in a 24-hour period, or when otherwise required by the state minimum fire safety standards, the owner or manager of the facility shall notify the on-duty officer of the fire department by contacting the non-emergency number at the E911 Center (770-445-2117). Additionally, the owner or manager must conduct a fire watch during the entire time that the life safety system is out of service or when otherwise required by the state minimum fire safety standards in accordance with the provisions of subsection (b) of this section.
