(1) Persons assigned to fire watch should be familiar with the building or premises and have access to all areas to sufficiently perform their patrol duties. Assigned persons should also be well-versed in any and all emergency evacuation procedures, safety plans, alarm activation procedures, and have formal training in the proper use of fire extinguishers or other emergency safety equipment.
